              "detail": "During the later Ming period, tax reforms increasingly converted obligations into payments in silver. Revenue helped support the state and its military. Farmers often needed access to markets to obtain silver. This example precedes Qing rule in Beijing; silver did not replace every tax or transaction everywhere."
